course: dictionary
lesson: 3717
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, so context tells you which one the writer means. «Tom flicked his ruler at Lily to make his mates laugh» means a quick, light hit, because of the ruler, Lily and the laughing mates.
explain: «Flick the classroom light on and off» uses flick to mean switch something on or off quickly. Try your meaning in the sentence: "switch the light on and off quickly" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: A snake «flicks its tongue to pick up smells from the air». The snake is not hitting anything; it is making a quick, small movement. Animals use flick in other ways too: a horse can flick its tail, and a tarantula flicks itchy hairs at its enemies.
explain: Flicking things at people is rude and can hurt eyes, so use the word with care. A dictionary will give you the other meanings, such as flicking through a book, or the old British word «the flicks» for the cinema.
fact: Flick can be a verb or a noun: you can flick a finger, or give a flick of the wrist.
fact: «Flick» means to move or hit something with a quick, small movement.
fact: «Flick» means to switch something on or off quickly, as in «flick the light switch».
fact: «Flick through» means to turn the pages of a book or magazine quickly.
fact: «The flicks» is an informal, old UK word for the cinema.
exercise: «A snake flicks its tongue to pick up smells from the air.» What does flicks mean here? | Makes a loud noise | Sleeps in the sun | Swallows its food whole | *Moves quickly with a small movement
exercise: What does «flick the light switch» mean? | Paint the switch bright red | Carry the switch heavily | *Switch the light on or off quickly | Clean the switch very carefully
exercise: «With a flick of the wrist, she caught the ball.» Is flick a noun or a verb in this sentence? | Verb | *Noun | Adjective | Adverb
test: «Most American tarantulas flick itchy barbed hairs at enemies.» What does flick mean here? | Sleep through the night | *A quick hit or movement | Burn brightly | Wash gently
test: Ella wants to read the comic quickly. What does «flick through» mean? | Buy a new comic | Tear it into pieces | *Turn the pages quickly | Read every word slowly
exam: Old UK people used «the flicks» to mean what? | A bus stop | A school playground | A football pitch | *A cinema
